@fcotrading @DanielTNiles Since Jesus doesn’t trade the VIX, there’s no prophecy in these trades. They’re just bets. Unfollow the accounts hyping every “huge” macro trade like it means something. Most of the time, it doesn’t. On individual stocks, big trades can actually matter.

@theinvestor999 @DanielTNiles When the VIX starts moving higher, then start doing something. I’m not saying we can’t get a 2–3% drawdown. That’s normal. But right now, I just don’t see the setup for a major correction. What’s the catalyst? If a new catalyst appears, then reassess.

It’s a fair question, and it is possible, although it happens less often in an algo-driven market. In the old days, markets would digest information more slowly. Today, algos extrapolate many moves ahead and often go full force on day one once they think they understand what the new information means.
